/**
 * Gap fill (September 2026): entities the corpus lacked relative to the goal of complete
 * oncology coverage. See docs/GAPS.md for the audit that produced this file.
 *
 *  - gapCancers (src/data/spikes/gap-cancers.ts): 32 cancers with baseline records
 *  - products: approved oncology drugs, diagnostics and supportive agents that were missing
 *  - targets: antigens, kinases and checkpoints referenced by approved or late-stage agents
 *  - technologies: supportive, survivorship and access-related care as first-class objects
 *  - terms and collections: guideline bodies, programmes and patient organisations
 *
 * Wire up with `import { gapFill } from "./gap-fill";` and `...gapFill,` in ALL_INPUTS.
 * All ids are checked against the existing corpus for collisions (scripts/validate-additions pattern).
 */
